cat > data/about.md <<'EOF'
# About this app

This is a minimal retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) demo. A web page sends your question to a Python server, which finds relevant text in local files and passes it to a language model.

## Adding documents

Put Markdown or plain text files in the documents folder, then restart the backend. Documents are read and indexed only once, at startup.
EOF
cat > data/retrieval.md <<'EOF'
# How retrieval works

Documents are split into chunks on blank lines. Retrieval ranks the chunks with BM25, a classic keyword scoring formula, and returns at most three of them.

## Limits

Keyword search does not match synonyms. Use words that appear in the documents.
EOF
